# Production build configuration.
#
# Vite loads .env first and layers .env.production on top, so a key defined in
# .env is NOT unset by omitting it here — it has to be overridden explicitly.
# This file used to omit VITE_API_URL_PROD "so the local build falls back to
# /api/v1", but the fallback never ran: .env supplies the Render URL, so
# `npm run build && npm run preview` pointed at the live deployment and every
# request died on CORS.
#
# /api/v1 is relative, so the preview server's proxy (vite.config.ts → preview)
# forwards it to the local Django on :8000.
#
# Real deployments set VITE_API_URL_PROD in the platform's env vars (Render,
# Vercel). Variables already present in the environment take priority over
# every .env file, so that override still wins over this line.
VITE_ENV=production
VITE_API_URL_PROD=/api/v1
